<article class="env-lemma" id="0A7X">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0A7X">Lemma <span data-tag="0A7X">47.17.1</span>.</a> Let $A$ be a Noetherian ring. Let $\mathfrak p$ be a minimal prime of $A$. Then $H^ i(\omega _ A^\bullet )_\mathfrak p$ is nonzero for exactly one $i$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The complex $\omega _ A^\bullet \otimes _ A A_\mathfrak p$ is a dualizing complex for $A_\mathfrak p$ (Lemma <a href="/tag/0A7G" data-tag="0A7G">47.15.6</a>). The dimension of $A_\mathfrak p$ is zero as $\mathfrak p$ is minimal. Hence the result follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/0A7R" data-tag="0A7R">47.16.8</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>